Rem --- Setup Screen --- 
Close Workbench 
Screen Open 0,640,256,16,Lowres

Flash Off : Curs Off : Hide On 

Palette 0,$0,$FFF,$F00,$F0

Rem --- Correct Buffer Command for AMOS Pro ---
Set Sprite Buffer 256

Rem --- Draw a 16x16 box on the screen --- 
Ink 2
Bar 0,0 To 16,16
Ink 1
Bar 5,5 To 12,12
Ink 5
Bar 7,7 To 8,8
Rem --- Correct Get Sprite Syntax using "To" --- 
Get Sprite 1,0,0 To 16,16
Rem --- Clear screen to prove it is a hardware sprite ---
Cls 0
Rem --- Display the grabbed sprite --- 
X=150
Y=70

X1=450
Y1=90
Y16=Y*16

Rem its a little shaking 


DY16=4
For I=0 To 300
'here if we have I/2 it creates a shaking effect 
Sprite Update Off 
DY=0

If I mod 3=0 Then DY=1
Y=Y+DY
Y16=Y16+4

Print Y,

Rem Sprite 1,X+I,Y16/16,1
Sprite 1,X+I,Y,1
Sprite 4,X1-I,Y,1
Rem Sprite 4,
Sprite Update 

Wait Vbl 

Next 

Wait Key 
